course: dictionary
lesson: 8065
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it. «Try to relax before the test.» Here relax means rest and become calm, not worried. The clue is the test, which can make you feel worried.
explain: «Relax your arms and let them hang loose.» Here relax means let a muscle go soft and not tight. The clue is arms, which are part of your body. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Relax can also mean make a rule less strict. «The school will relax the rule about phones.» The clue is rule. Relax is a verb, so it changes: relaxes, relaxed, relaxing.
fact: «Relax» means to rest and become calm and less worried or busy.
fact: To relax your body or a muscle means to let it go loose and soft, not tight, as in «Looking at something far away lets the focusing muscles of the eyes relax.»
fact: To relax a rule means to make it less strict.
fact: Ways to relax when you feel worried or angry include slow deep breathing, counting, stretching, reading, listening to music and being outside.
fact: Relax changes its form: relaxes, relaxed, relaxing.
exercise: «After a busy day, Sam sat on the sofa to relax.» What does relax mean here? | *Rest and become calm | Argue loudly with his sister | Run fast around the park
exercise: «Shake out your hands and let your shoulder relax.» What does relax mean here? | Hide the shoulder | Lift the shoulder high | *Let the muscle go loose and soft | Make the shoulder stronger
exercise: Ms Okafor says, «The school will relax the rule about phones.» What does relax mean here? | Write the rule on the board | Shout the rule loudly | Break the rule on purpose | *Make the rule less strict
test: «Take slow, deep breaths when you feel angry, and then try to relax.» What does relax mean here? | Shout at your friend | *Become calm and less worried | Get very angry | Jump up and down
test: Which word is the past form of relax? | *relaxed | relaxing | relaxes | relax
exam: Which sentence uses relax to mean make a rule less strict? | «Try some slow breathing to relax.» | «Relax your fingers and let them drop.» | «Just relax, we have plenty of time.» | *«The club will relax its rule about late arrivals.»
